    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d850">

                <pb facs="0833" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg729"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6325b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-22T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 22, 1913—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. Department’s February 21, 11 p.m. In next to last paragraph the words
                    “damages to American property on account of the recent political disturbances”
                    of course refer to this whole period of disturbances.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
